From 29fb58af0c5bda4b3cc9a31c066c641af8eb7ef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 14:24:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] policy routing: fix the six field defects + rwatch self-heals
 the ip-rule half

- WGC target could reboot the box: the emitted pbr_skip_add now refuses a full
  8-slot blog skip table BEFORE writing, uses the vendor byte form (printf, no
  trailing newline), and gates on the wgc interface being up
- Apply-and-Confirm race: armed=0 is cleared BEFORE nvram_commit so a reboot
  can never resurrect a phantom "awaiting confirmation"
- fresh boxes seed an honest disabled baseline (empty lastgood no longer
  defeats the refuse-apply guard); armed card warns Confirm-to-persist (RVR_63)
- firewall-start addons run LAST, after the PBR re-apply block, so their rules
  are not reordered/lost by Reaper re-inserting its chains
- rwatch now heals lost ip rules too: the generator writes expect_rules and
  rwatch re-applies under the existing 120s throttle when the live count drops
- target dropdown hides unconfigured OVPN/WGC (new ov[] in the pbr cfg JSON),
  flags configured-but-down; bounded arm poll replaces the single 1.5s shot

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
